    <string name="format_hint">A page of that paper then gets its exact proportions, and the PDF its size. Receipts, cards and other shapes keep their own.</string>
    <string name="choice_title">Which engine?</string>
    <string name="choice_intro">Two ways of finding the page and reading its text. Both work on the phone: your documents are never sent to be read.</string>
    <string name="choice_google">Google ML Kit (recommended)</string>
    <string name="choice_google_body">Finds and straightens pages most surely, on any background, and reads text very well. Closed Google code: it needs Google Play services and sends usage statistics to Google (not your documents). Latin script only: Russian is read by Tesseract.</string>
    <string name="choice_google_missing">Not available on this phone: Google Play services are missing.</string>
    <string name="choice_free">Open source</string>
    <string name="choice_free_body">The app\'s own page finder and Tesseract: free software, nothing goes to Google, seven languages. Less sure of the page on pale backgrounds (the corners are easy to adjust), blurred shots are flagged at once.</string>
    <string name="choice_later">You can change this at any time in the settings.</string>
